&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roblox&#39;s Object Store team is building the in-house, multi-tenant object storage platform that underpins every large-object workload at Roblox — assets, media, analytics, backups, and machine learning datasets — at exabyte scale, trillions of objects, and terabytes per second of throughput. We build and run it ourselves on bare metal in our own data centers, replacing cloud object storage with a platform we control end to end — down to the hardware. As a principal engineer on the Object Store team, you will shape the architecture, build and launch the capabilities that keep this platform durable, fast, and efficient at global scale, and set the technical direction for where it goes next. You will report to the Engineering Manager for Storage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and build the object store&lt;/strong&gt; — S3-compatible gateway, metadata and indexing, data placement and tiering, multi-tenancy and isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the technical strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: multi-year architecture, build-vs-buy calls, and the migration off cloud object storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve the control plane&lt;/strong&gt; for elastic scaling, autonomous healing, self-service provisioning, and zero-downtime tenant moves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the bare-metal fleet at scale&lt;/strong&gt; — cluster lifecycle, upgrades, rebalancing, failure domains, hardware and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile and optimize&lt;/strong&gt; critical data paths; drive down tail latency and cost per byte.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish engineering best practices&lt;/strong&gt; — design reviews, benchmarks, failure drills, post-incident retrospectives — targeting 4+ 9s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate everything&lt;/strong&gt;: testing, CI/CD, rollout safety, observability, autoscaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor engineers and partner cross-functionally&lt;/strong&gt; with security, analytics, and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of experience in software engineering or a relevant field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience building and operating &lt;strong&gt;large-scale distributed storage&lt;/strong&gt; — object stores, blob stores, or distributed file systems — at petabyte scale or beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience &lt;strong&gt;running an object storage platform in production&lt;/strong&gt;: data placement and rebalancing, erasure coding, cluster tuning, and upgrades at scale. Depth operating these systems matters more here than contributing to their internals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in &lt;strong&gt;C++, Go, or Rust&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of &lt;strong&gt;durability and replication&lt;/strong&gt; — erasure coding, geo-replication, consistency trade-offs, blast-radius containment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success shipping &lt;strong&gt;high-throughput, low-latency services on bare-metal, on-prem fleets&lt;/strong&gt; with strong observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn ambiguous requirements into a clear roadmap and &lt;strong&gt;influence cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for &lt;strong&gt;automation, rigorous testing, and data-driven decisions&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt; upstream contributions to open-source storage projects; S3 API compatibility at scale, NVMe/HDD tiering, or migrating large workloads off public-cloud object storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$295,250&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$345,040 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roblox’s data platform powers analytics, ML, and product decisions for a platform serving 200M+ daily active users. As a &lt;strong&gt;Principal Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; in the &lt;strong&gt;Data Platform Orchestration&lt;/strong&gt; team, you will be the technical leader for the system that schedules and runs the company’s data workloads. Our team owns Apache Airflow and the Kubernetes (EKS) infrastructure underneath it, running 8,000+ DAGs every day, most of them Spark jobs. You will set the long-term architecture for how Roblox orchestrates data at scale, and you will be hands-on in making it faster, more reliable, and easier for hundreds of engineers to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the Orchestration Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the multi-year architecture for Airflow and the surrounding platform, including scheduler and executor design, multi-tenancy, upgrades and migrations, and where the platform should evolve next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale and Harden Airflow:&lt;/strong&gt; Find and remove scaling limits across the scheduler, metadata database, executors, and DAG parsing. Make sure thousands of daily DAGs run with predictable latency and strong SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Orchestration on Kubernetes:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the design and operation of our EKS clusters for orchestration and Spark workloads, including autoscaling, resource isolation, cost efficiency, and deployment automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Platform Tooling for Internal Engineers:&lt;/strong&gt; Design the APIs, custom operators and providers, libraries, and self-service tooling that let data teams build, deploy, and monitor pipelines safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Observability and Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish SLOs, alerting, and diagnostics for pipelines and platform components. Lead incident reviews and fix the root causes in code, not just in runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Across Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with data platform, governance, data science, and product engineering teams to align roadmaps, guide technical decisions, and build consensus on complex initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the Engineering Bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Set standards for code quality, design, and operational readiness. Mentor staff, senior, and mid-level engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. equivalent in CS or sufficient experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience designing, building, and operating production-grade, large-scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow Orchestration Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep, hands-on experience designing, running, and scaling a production data-related workflow orchestrator or job scheduler (thousands of workflows or DAGs a day). Apache Airflow is ideal, but experience with an equivalent system (Dagster, Prefect, Temporal, or a large in-house scheduler) is also welcome. You understand scheduler and executor design, metadata store performance, task isolation, retries and idempotency, and safe upgrades and migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience managing and scaling production Kubernetes clusters on AWS (EKS), including Helm, autoscaling (Karpenter or Cluster Autoscaler), and GitOps-style deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency in Python, plus Go or Java, with a record of writing clean, well-tested platform and tooling code. You are a software engineer who builds and improves systems, not someone who mainly handles tickets and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Workload Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of how Spark jobs run on Kubernetes (Spark on K8s, spark-operator, or EMR on EKS) and how orchestration interacts with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience building platforms used by other engineers, with strong instincts for APIs, observability, reliability, and developer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Organizational Technical Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; A track record of influencing direction across a large engineering organization and driving multi-quarter projects from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extreme Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You define the problem when requirements are unclear, unblock dependencies, and see complex work through to stable production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus Points:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to Apache Airflow or related open-source projects (Airflow providers, Helm chart, spark-operator, Karpenter, Argo CD).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with other orchestration systems (Dagster, Temporal, Argo Workflows, Flyte) and the judgment to know when each fits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Terraform or other infrastructure-as-code, Prometheus/OpenTelemetry, and cost optimization or chargeback for shared platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating infrastructure at consumer-internet scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$295,250&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$345,040 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
