&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Trust and Safety Operations team is focused (ok, maybe obsessed) on scaling Roblox’s Operations organization and transforming our customer experience through our multi-year vision and strategy execution. Creators are the engine of Roblox. When something breaks for them, whether it is a broken publish flow, a payout that didn&#39;t land, an asset that won&#39;t upload, how quickly and how well we resolve it directly shapes whether they keep building with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be reporting to the Trust &amp;amp; Safety India Operations Manager. The team provides support to Roblox’s global players, developers, and advertisers. As a Senior Product Support Specialist on our Safety Ops Team, you’ll own the hardest escalations end to end, drive root cause analysis with engineering and product partners, and then close the loop by turning what you learn into support content that scales for both our human agents and our automated support experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additionally, you will serve as a product expert working closely with the Product Support Management team, providing detailed synthesis of new and existing issues our users experience to prioritize and enable engineering teams to improve the platform. You&#39;ll operate with a high degree of independence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support health and proactive gap identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-monitor the health of creator support: contact drivers, resolution rates, reopen and escalation rates, deflection performance, CSAT, and where creators are getting stuck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mine ticket, content, and automation data for patterns: recurring issues, missing coverage, misleading documentation, product gaps and surface them proactively with a recommendation attached to the PSM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently own root cause analysis for complex, high-impact, and ambiguous creator issues including ones that cross product, platform, and policy boundaries..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get ahead of launches: review upcoming product and policy changes, pressure test them from a support perspective, and make sure content, tooling, and agent readiness are in place before creators feel the change. Support PSM in preparing RCA or post launch report to surface to all concerned stakeholder (engineering, product, operations etc)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report clearly and regularly to support and product leadership on where creator support is strong, where it&#39;s degrading, and what you propose to do about it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence in how creator support runs: hold the line on quality standards, tighten workflows and handoffs between support, engineering, and product, eliminate manual toil through better process and tooling, and treat every process change as something to be measured rather than assumed. Where the current way of working is the bottleneck, you name it and fix it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Feedback Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with Product Managers (PMs) during alpha/beta testing phases to provide a &quot;Supportability Scorecard&quot; for major upcoming platform features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Support Content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and maintain the authoritative internal knowledge base agents rely on which includes but is not restricted to troubleshooting guides, decision trees, macros, policy interpretations and keep it accurate as the product changes underneath it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own creator support content, which includes (but is not limited to) intent-ready articles, structured resolution paths, and clear, unambiguous source material for support agents to rely on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation and self-service experiences, supplying the content and acting as a subject-matter judgment behind them, and flagging where automation is producing wrong or incomplete answers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior point of contact during high-severity creator-facing incidents, coordinating across support, engineering, and comms, when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar on escalation quality across the team by setting the standard for what a well-formed escalation looks like, and reduce the volume that shouldn&#39;t have escalated in the first place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;br&gt;You Have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in technical support, product support, or a comparable operational role, including significant time at a senior or escalation tier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of independent root cause analysis on complex technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication. You have the ability to explain a nuanced technical failure to an engineer and to a frustrated creator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and genuine self-direction. You choose your own problems, defend your prioritization, and close things out without being managed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional influence without authority, you can get engineering and product to care about a support problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning support content at scale, with real evidence that your content changed outcomes (deflection, handle time, resolution quality).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing or structuring content balancing automation driven human in the loop support, self-service, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience supporting a developer, creator, or partner audience rather than a general consumer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Roblox as a creation platform; Studio, Lua, the developer economy or comparable experience with a UGC platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Diagnostic Proficiency: Comfortable querying datasets (SQL, Tableau, or similar BI tools) and analyzing diagnostic logs to isolate bugs before routing to engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Roblox Live&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox Live &lt;strong&gt;creates the moments that bring Roblox together&lt;/strong&gt;. We turn music, entertainment, culture, and the creativity of our community into new ways to play and connect. From major platform celebrations to live performances and breakout creator moments, we give players something to show up for, experience with friends, and come back to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a small, fast-moving team with the ambition to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;shape the future of live experiences on Roblox&lt;/strong&gt;. We bring ideas to life with creators and partners, build the technology that makes them possible, and turn what works into tools that let the creator community take it further.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Program Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to turn our slate of live experiences into a coordinated program. You will own the calendar, cross-team dependencies, budget ask, risk register, executive communications, and post-event playbooks. You will help shape new programs early, bringing ideas on formats and audience hooks, then build the plan that takes them through launch and learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role for someone who can turn ambiguity into a plan and lead across teams through trust and judgment. You’ll work closely with creative, content, product, engineering, marketing, safety, and external partners. You’ll align the program around shared goals, partner with the Live Ops Producer on launch readiness and event-day escalations, and give leadership a clear view of progress and decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You Will:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn the programming slate into a forward calendar with clear phases, milestones, decision gates, and owners. Manage dependencies and resource conflicts across events in concept, production, and live operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define each program’s audience, goals, and success measures. Bring creative and operational judgment to early concepts, and make practical recommendations on scope, sequencing, and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain one shared view of program status. Establish how workstream owners update plans, track commitments, and resolve blockers across internal teams and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run focused planning sessions, workstream reviews, and recaps that keep decisions moving. Partner with technical leads on feasibility and with the Live Ops Producer on readiness milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate staffing, studio, vendor, and production estimates into a program budget request. Partner with Finance and workstream owners to track commitments, spend, and changes against the approved plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the risk register, including assumptions, issues, dependencies, and mitigation plans. Assign owners, surface risks early, and recommend changes that protect the program’s goals and delivery dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give executives concise updates on outcomes, progress, risks, and decisions needed. Give workstream owners the detail they need to act, with clear commitments and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish decision owners and escalation paths before launch. Support the Live Ops Producer during live events by resolving cross-team dependencies and coordinating leadership decisions and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead retrospectives and publish post-event readouts with Data Science and functional leads. Track program results, partner contributions, and creative concepts against the goals set before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn lessons and operating runbooks into reusable program playbooks. Track follow-up actions and improve planning, handoffs, and reporting so each event starts with what the team has already learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in program management, production, or live operations, including 3+ years leading live events, recurring content programs, or partner programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and running complex programs across creative, technical, and business teams, with multiple initiatives moving at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience consolidating budget requests, tracking program financials, and managing risks and dependencies through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment about scope, priorities, and escalation, with the ability to make progress before every detail is settled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead without formal authority and build lasting trust with internal teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear writing and executive communication, with experience connecting program activity to measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with program management tools such as Jira, Airtable, Asana, or equivalents, and the ability to build practical tracking and reporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in gaming, creator platforms, entertainment, live events, or esports (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a program or operating model from scratch that other teams adopted (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Roblox and its player and creator communities (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating partner programs or creative concepts through shared goals and scorecards (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,940&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,840 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Security Auditor on our Internal Audit team, you will play a pivotal role in leading IT risk evaluations, audits, and readiness exercises across Roblox&#39;s dynamic internal technology environment. In this role, you will champion information security and privacy compliance while helping scale our operational objectives. We are looking for an innovative security auditor with strong technical foundations who can design and build cutting-edge, AI-integrated audit programs. Reporting directly to the IT Audit Senior Manager, you will partner closely with key cross-functional teams—including Engineering, Information Security, Legal, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, and Finance—to shape a secure and resilient ecosystem at Roblox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and operationalize an audit program to meet the cybersecurity audit requirements of the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) regulations, including scoping, risk assessment, gap analysis, audit execution, remediation tracking, and reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize AI tools and offshore resources to test the design and operating effectiveness of controls across the cybersecurity control domains, including access controls, data classifications, vulnerability management, production engineering security, cloud security, data security, end-point security, network security, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute and support privacy audits to address regulatory requirements and to help management benchmark against industry best practices, identify ways to enhance the overall compliance posture, and streamline processes through automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conceive and lead ad hoc analyses of IT &amp;amp; Information security data to support risk-based operational audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable methods to ensure consistency in results, maintain an up-to-date understanding of evolving regulatory landscapes, and help develop a robust internal knowledge base on security compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the identification and implementation of new processes/controls required by regulatory compliance frameworks, and the remediation of corrective action plans relating to audit findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop audit reports by summarizing audit findings and associated risks, identifying action owners, and aligning on remediation plans with management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with XFN teams (including Engineering, Information Security, Legal, Trust &amp;amp; Safety and Finance) to help create integrated compliance requirements for Roblox&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with internal automation efforts and tool implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Technology, Information Systems, Computer Science or a related technical field of study or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years professional IT audit experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years security audit or security compliance experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid technical knowledge in multiple security and privacy compliance frameworks including: CCPA, NIST, ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance and risk management skills, CISSP, CISM, CIPP, CISA Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beginner to intermediate knowledge of scripting languages such as structured query language, Python, Shell scripting etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools in audit testings and daily operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$204,580 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a founding member of the Security Operations team in EMEA, you will join us at an exciting time in Roblox’s SIRT &amp;amp; SOC program. You will design and build the detections, automation and tooling that let a lean team monitor and protect players, developers, employees and the platform at global scale and serve as security incident commander in the region. This is a highly autonomous role where you will be a primary decision-maker, core to our mission to maintain a highly capable 24/7/365 monitoring and response capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While you will work in close collaboration with peers at our US West Coast Headquarters, the time difference requires an engineer who can operate independently, making critical decisions without immediate oversight. We favor engineering our way out of toil through automation, orchestration, detections-as-code, and risk-based prioritization,&amp;nbsp;while retaining the deep technical skills required to conduct detailed, hands-on analysis and lead response end-to-end when the situation warrants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based in London, UK. You will be working from a dedicated, private space located within a shared office environment, designed to enable collaboration while remaining secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Detection &amp;amp; Response Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, write, and maintain production-quality detections, automations and integrations (detections-as-code, SOAR playbooks, data and enrichment pipelines) that scale our monitoring capability and reduce manual toil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Tooling &amp;amp; Platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and improve the tooling the global SIRT/SOC depends on alert quality and enrichment, case-management integrations and automation that powers reliable &quot;follow-the-sun&quot; hand-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise High Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary Incident Commander for the European time zone, making critical, time-sensitive decisions independently before US HQ comes online. You will serve as the senior-most security engineering point of contact in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Strategy &amp;amp; Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape the technical direction of the detection &amp;amp; response engineering function, specifically architecting how global hand-offs and &quot;follow-the-sun&quot; models can be optimized and automated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command Security Incidents:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure serious threats and impacts are understood, mitigated, and learned from with speed and professionalism, often leading responses end-to-end without immediate escalation paths during local hours — and turning what you learn into durable, automated detections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct Forensic Investigations &amp;amp; Threat Hunt:&lt;/strong&gt; Dig into complex context to determine whether threats exist, take decisive action and proactively hunt for anomalous activity in our signals, distinguishing outliers from threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead High-Profile Responses:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Security and Engineering to lead responses to major vulnerabilities or platform-wide events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate Cross-Functionally:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Legal, HR, Executive teams, and external partners (Developers &amp;amp; Customers). You will also travel semi-regularly to the USA to visit HQ, ensuring deep alignment with central engineering and security leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years across security engineering, Infosec, IT, Infra/SRE, and/or Incident Response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specialization:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years specifically in Detection or Response, with a track record of &lt;em&gt;building&lt;/em&gt;, writing detections, automation or security tooling, not solely operating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable writing and reviewing production-quality code (Scripting) and building automations, integrations and data pipelines that others depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to work independently in satellite offices or distributed teams. You are comfortable being the &quot;person in charge&quot; during your shift and making calls that impact the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Extensive experience operating as an incident commander. You can flex into deep engineering work but also possess the executive presence to coordinate responders and communicate status to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investigations:&lt;/strong&gt; Expert-level capability investigating threats in enterprise and production environments, taking ownership from identification to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge/Tools/Techniques:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of security tooling (SIEM, EDR, IDS/IPS, NDR, SOAR) and experience extending or building on it. You are proficient in applying Incident Response frameworks (NIST IR Lifecycle, Cyber Kill Chain, MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK) to real-world scenarios, and you collaborate effectively with engineering colleagues, leveraging extensive expertise across infrastructure and technologies (Public Cloud, OS, Virtualization, Containerization, Networking, Build/Development infrastructure, and Hardware).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a related technical field; advanced degree preferred or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Builder-Operator:&lt;/strong&gt; You would rather automate a problem out of existence than staff around it and you hold yourself to an engineering bar even under incident pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Strategic Self-Starter:&lt;/strong&gt; You don&#39;t wait for instructions. You identify gaps in coverage — especially those unique to regional or time-zone-specific challenges — and fix them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Detailed Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You enjoy exploring the details and considering the second- and third-order effects of your decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Eager Problem Solver:&lt;/strong&gt; You are drawn to complex issues rather than avoidant of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emboldened to Make Change:&lt;/strong&gt; You instinctively ask what you can do to improve the situation rather than waiting to be prompted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compelled by our Mission:&lt;/strong&gt; You are driven by the opportunity to protect our community and the safe space we&#39;ve created.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Calculated Risk Taker:&lt;/strong&gt; You move fast, navigating reasonable risks to take action and build capabilities as quickly as possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
