&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox Studio is the creation engine behind millions of immersive 3D games built by creators around the world. We are entering a major platform transition, evolving Studio into an AI-Native IDE where intelligent systems plan, act, validate, and iterate alongside creators to amplify their output. We are seeking a Technical Director, Applied AI to own the technical direction of the agentic AI systems embedded deeply into Roblox Studio. This is a hands-on individual-contributor role operating at the intersection of platform engineering, AI systems, and developer experience, where you will set the technical direction, design the architecture, and write the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and build&lt;/strong&gt; the agentic AI systems at the core of the AI-Native IDE (planning, execution, validation, evaluation) so they are production-grade and reliable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide how Studio uses&lt;/strong&gt; coding models, agents, retrieval, tool calling, and context management across the Assistant and the broader creator workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the quality bar and evaluation strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, standing up quantitative and qualitative eval pipelines, including human-in-the-loop, so we ship with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize these systems&lt;/strong&gt; for latency, throughput, and cost (caching, routing, distillation, quantization).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring reusable patterns and best practices&lt;/strong&gt; to teams across Studio, raising the applied-AI fluency of Studio engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12+ years of engineering experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including ownership of large-scale, long-lived platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep, hands-on experience&lt;/strong&gt; building LLM-powered and agentic systems in production, beyond chat-based interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong systems and software engineering skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to design the architecture and write the code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of defining evaluation frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; for AI product quality, combining automated metrics with human review, and optimizing inference for latency, throughput, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong background in developer tools&lt;/strong&gt; or IDE-like platforms, with a proven ability to set technical direction and raise quality across multiple teams as an individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/em&gt; Background in coding models or code-generation systems, and/or research experience in reinforcement learning (RLHF, RLAIF, preference modeling) or related model-training techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An innovative technical leader&lt;/strong&gt; who wants to build the AI systems that power the creativity of millions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-minded&lt;/strong&gt;, with a real understanding of developer needs, creator workflows, and how AI systems land in the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable and curious&lt;/strong&gt;, with good judgment about when to build, when to reuse, and when to push a need back to a model team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Able to operate at the deepest technical levels&lt;/strong&gt; and still communicate direction clearly to partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$399,420&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$457,970 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Vendor Operations focused on automation, you will work horizontally across our safety vendor ecosystem to drive programs that standardize, automate, and scale the processes that keep our operations running. Rather than owning a single vendor relationship in isolation, you will operate across systems, tools, and vendor partners to build repeatable workflows, introduce automation and LLM-based tooling where it drives efficiency, and establish the reporting and communication rhythms that keep senior leadership informed. This is a builder&#39;s role for someone equally comfortable in a vendor business review, a process-mapping session, and a dataset full of operational signals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead horizontal programs that scale safety vendor operations by identifying friction across systems and vendor relationships, then designing and rolling out standardized processes and playbooks that improve quality, throughput, and cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with vendors and internal stakeholders to translate operational goals into concrete workflows, SLAs, and success metrics, holding programs accountable to measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement automation opportunities across manual and repetitive processes, including agentic and LLM-based solutions that reduce toil and increase consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reporting that turns large, messy operational datasets into clear signals, including trend analyses and program-health metrics leadership can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and deliver crisp communications and updates for senior leadership, synthesizing program status, risks, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a connective layer across vendor operations, tooling, and cross-functional partners (Global Scaled Operations, Moderation, Customer Support, Legal, Finance, and Engineering), ensuring changes are coordinated and scaled rather than solved one-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You have:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of program and/or project management experience, ideally in operations, vendor management, or a trust &amp;amp; safety-related environment (experience interacting with vendors or customer service operations is a strong plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A programmatic, systems-level mindset - you naturally look for the reusable process behind a one-off problem and know how to drive adoption across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience automating processes, plus practical familiarity with leveraging LLMs for agentic solutions and a working understanding of basic machine learning concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or exposure to vendor relationship management, including SLAs, performance reviews, escalations, and partnering to improve delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in spreadsheet software (Excel/Google Sheets) and strong data fluency, with the ability to work with large datasets and turn them into reports and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with a proven track record of drafting materials for and communicating with senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic proficiency in a coding or scripting language (e.g., Python, SQL) to independently explore and contextualize large datasets is preferred, but not mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive mindset with the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative, global team setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$144,620&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$174,100 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and driven early-career professional to join us as a Workplace Experience Coordinator for a part-time, one-year fixed-term contract in our Korea office. In this role, you will help create a seamless and engaging workplace experience for our Korea team, supporting a range of areas including workplace operations, employee onboarding, vendor coordination, and internal events. You will work closely with the local team and external partners to keep our workplace running smoothly and contribute to a collaborative, welcoming, and productive office environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Office Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Help ensure the Korea office runs smoothly and efficiently by coordinating workplace needs, managing office resources and inventory, and partnering with facility providers on maintenance and operational requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion the Employee Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Support a welcoming and productive workplace experience, including new hire onboarding, workspace readiness, and coordination of team activities and gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide Administrative &amp;amp; EA Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage visitor registration, coordinate meeting room logistics, and handle shipping and courier support. You will maintain essential office documentation (SOPs, inventory lists, contact directories) and provide ad-hoc administrative support for team meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Internal Events &amp;amp; Team Engagement: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to internal events and team initiatives from planning through execution. This may include participating in ideation and planning, coordinating logistics and vendors, and providing on-site support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide Flexible Cross-Functional Support:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with the Korea team on evolving office and team priorities, stepping in where needed to help initiatives run smoothly and effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of experience in facility management or office administration within a fast-paced environment is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in both Korean and English to effectively collaborate with local teams, vendors, and global headquarters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills with proficiency in Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship or experience in an office environment, administration, hospitality, or customer service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A basic understanding of vendor coordination, event planning, or invoice tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Roblox and an understanding of its platform, community, and culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driven &amp;amp; Eager to Learn:&lt;/strong&gt; You are highly motivated to kickstart your corporate career, quick to absorb new information, and excited to take on new challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly Organized:&lt;/strong&gt; You have an exceptional attention to detail and can seamlessly manage multiple priorities, from daily administrative tasks to event logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hospitality-Driven:&lt;/strong&gt; You possess a service-oriented mentality, taking pride in creating a welcoming, inclusive, and productive environment for all employees and visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Problem Solver:&lt;/strong&gt; You are proactive, resourceful, and capable of finding creative solutions to unexpected workplace challenges while exhibiting grace under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative &amp;amp; Adaptable:&lt;/strong&gt; You thrive in a fast-paced environment, are comfortable navigating change, and are always willing to roll up your sleeves to ensure the success of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where You&#39;ll Be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an onsite part time role based in the Seoul office, where you’ll be expected to work in the office 3 days (Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) a week. The working hours will typically be 1:30 PM–6:00 PM, with some flexibility required to accommodate business needs, including occasional morning hours&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Global Partner will be responsible for supporting office services, facilities operations, workplace amenities, and employee experience across Roblox’s smaller domestic and international offices. The role will establish consistency and parity with Roblox headquarters by ensuring employees have access to reliable workplace services, functional amenities, appropriate resources, and a consistent level of support regardless of where they work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will serve as a strategic partner and liaison among Facilities and Workplaces, People , Finance, Corporate Engineering, Global Security, local office leaders, landlords, property managers, vendors, and other internal stakeholders. The Global Partner will independently assess office needs, identify service gaps, coordinate solutions, and establish operating standards that reflect the workplace experience provided at Roblox headquarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When not traveling or directly supporting a remote office, this position will provide consistent support for headquarters projects and operations, including employee moves, office reconfigurations, workplace projects, safety initiatives, inspections, regulatory compliance, and other Facilities and Workplace priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at San Mateo HQ Monday–Friday, 9:00 AM–5:00 PM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support day-to-day facilities and workplace operations for Roblox’s smaller domestic and international offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary Facilities and Workplace point of contact for assigned global offices, providing responsive, consistent, and reliable operational support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain workplace standards that create greater parity between headquarters and remote offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the employee experience, facilities conditions, amenities, technology, security, safety, and operational needs of each assigned office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop office-specific action plans to address service gaps, operational risks, employee needs, and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Finance, Corporate Engineering, Global Security, local office leaders, landlords, property managers, and vendors to ensure each location is properly supported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure employees have access to functional workstations, meeting spaces, workplace technology, office supplies, amenities, and employee-facing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain office services by developing and documenting operating procedures, service standards, schedules, escalation paths, and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate preventive maintenance, repairs, inspections, testing, and facilities-related services with landlords and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce operational inconsistencies by establishing repeatable workplace programs, service expectations, and reporting practices across assigned offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and monitor service requests, response times, resolution times, vendor performance, recurring issues, and other workplace performance indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate unresolved issues and coordinate resources to ensure operational needs are addressed through completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support employee onboarding, offboarding, office access, workstation readiness, equipment coordination, and other workplace service requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate workplace programs, employee events, and office activities in partnership with Human Resources and local office leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support local emergency preparedness, workplace safety, incident response, and business-continuity requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure compliance with OSHA requirements, applicable building and fire codes, accessibility standards, local regulatory ordinances, and other workplace requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate required workplace inspections, permits, certifications, corrective actions, and compliance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular office assessments and document findings, risks, required actions, responsible parties, and completion dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support sustainability initiatives by identifying opportunities to reduce waste, conserve resources, improve energy efficiency, and promote responsible workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual budget planning, expense forecasting, purchase orders, invoices, accruals, and expenditure tracking for assigned offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare actual spending against approved budgets, identify variances, and recommend corrective actions when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support vendor sourcing, contract administration, invoicing, document control, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and Procurement to evaluate vendor proposals, service agreements, and operating costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review landlord and vendor responsibilities to ensure Roblox receives the services required under applicable agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain office documentation, service records, vendor information, emergency contacts, floor plans, equipment inventories, operating procedures, and compliance records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare regular updates for leadership summarizing office conditions, employee needs, operational performance, risks, costs, and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to domestic and international offices to assess conditions, develop local partnerships, implement standards, support projects, and confirm operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing remote support to global offices between onsite visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When not traveling, support headquarters projects, including employee moves, office reconfigurations, relocations, furniture changes, signage, workplace improvements, and space-readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the headquarters Facilities team with safety programs, inspections, regulatory compliance, emergency preparedness, and corrective-action tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support headquarters project teams with vendor coordination, scheduling, employee communications, site logistics, documentation, and operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide general administrative and operational support to Facilities project teams and local office leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the broader Facilities and Workplace team as business needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in facilities coordination, office services, workplace operations, global workplace support, or a related corporate environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience supporting multiple offices, including smaller domestic or international locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of office services, facilities operations, vendor coordination, workplace amenities, employee experience, and workplace safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering cross-functionally with Human Resources, Finance, Corporate Engineering or IT, Security, landlords, property managers, vendors, and business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently and take ownership of workplace needs without direct people-management responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional relationship-building and collaborative problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying service gaps, developing action plans, and driving operational issues through completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project-coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple offices, priorities, projects, and time zones simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and documenting operational procedures, service standards, escalation processes, and workplace programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of OSHA requirements, workplace safety practices, accessibility standards, building and fire codes, and other applicable regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with budget administration, forecasting, invoice management, purchase orders, contract documentation, and expense tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and track key performance indicators, analyze operational trends, and clearly communicate findings to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Workspace or similar business-productivity tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel domestically and internationally based on business and office needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, service-oriented, culturally aware, and calm under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to occasionally lift up to 25 pounds and perform physical tasks associated with workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace strategy and employee-experience program support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global facilities and workplace operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Office build-outs, renovations, expansions, relocations, and decommissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Moves, adds, and changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace safety, OSHA compliance, and emergency preparedness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lease administration and landlord coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget forecasting and financial management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project coordination and agile project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace data, reporting, and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor sourcing, contract administration, and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustainability and waste-reduction initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a globally distributed office portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across cultures, countries, and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Hours:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an onsite position (at HQ in San Mateo) scheduled five days per week, generally from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Domestic and international travel will be required based on business and office needs. On-call availability may be required to support global offices, urgent facilities matters, scheduled projects, safety incidents, and operational emergencies across multiple time zones.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$166,730 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Driven by a hospitality-first mindset and a commitment to attentive, personalized service, the Workplace Services Manager leads employee-facing workplace services and programs across Roblox’s San Mateo headquarters and satellite offices. Reporting to the Director of Facilities, this hands-on leader creates a welcoming, engaging, and consistently high-quality experience for Builders, guests, and visitors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns workplace hospitality, reception, employee events, service communications, and the everyday amenities that support a productive workplace. Partnering closely with People Services, Food &amp;amp; Beverage, Global Security, Facilities, and internal stakeholders, the Workplace Services Manager anticipates employee needs, resolves service concerns, and develops thoughtful programs that strengthen connection across Roblox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role partners with the Facilities Manager on issues affecting the employee experience. Technical maintenance, building systems, construction, and real estate planning remain within Facilities ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at San Mateo HQ Monday–Friday, 9:00 AM–6:00 PM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Hospitality &amp;amp; Service Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead daily employee-facing workplace services at Roblox HQ and support consistent service standards across satellite offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish hospitality standards for reception, visitor welcome, employee assistance, meeting support, and shared workplace amenities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reception areas, collaboration spaces, and common areas are welcoming, thoughtfully presented, and ready for use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace service requests through the Facilities Management System (FMS), ensuring timely responses, clear communication, and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use employee feedback and service data to identify recurring needs and improve responsiveness, satisfaction, and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employee communications about workplace services, amenities, events, and service interruptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer employee-facing parking services and ergonomics requests, coordinating with Facilities and other responsible teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global Security and Safety to deliver a welcoming arrival experience while following visitor access and safety procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Facilities to resolve maintenance concerns affecting employees and communicate progress through resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, benchmark, onboard, and manage workplace service vendors, including reception, office services, event support, and amenity providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear service expectations and evaluate vendors on responsiveness, presentation, employee satisfaction, and value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Services, IT, Executive Admins, Global Security, and department leaders to anticipate workplace needs and coordinate service delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate workplace welcome activities for new hires and support employee departures in partnership with People Services, IT, and Global Security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with property management on employee-facing services, shared amenities, and service communications, coordinating building maintenance matters through Facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track workplace services expenses, invoices, and contracts; prepare regular budget and service performance reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop service plans for executive meetings, visiting teams, and special gatherings, with clear ownership and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the planning and delivery of employee events, including Roblox Week, Hack Week, holiday events, intern programming, and happy hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop workplace programs that build community and support connection across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Food &amp;amp; Beverage Manager on the employee experience across cafés, coffee bars, and related amenities, incorporating feedback and coordinating event needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide attentive meeting and event support, including room readiness, catering coordination, signage, guest arrival, and onsite assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather Builder feedback through surveys, service interactions, and direct engagement; translate findings into practical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure workplace programs and communications consider the needs of employees across locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a hospitality-first culture that emphasizes anticipation, discretion, responsiveness, and consistent follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise and coach workplace services staff and service partners responsible for reception, employee assistance, office services, and event support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the team’s hospitality, communication, problem-solving, and service recovery skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish staffing coverage and service plans for daily operations, peak periods, and major employee events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain documented standards for employee interactions, visitor services, event delivery, and request resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage office supplies and employee-facing equipment, ensuring availability and coordinating repairs with the appropriate teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and track service measures, including response times, resolution times, employee satisfaction, and event feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Facilities, Food &amp;amp; Beverage, and Global Security to ensure clear handoffs and consistent employee support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available for evening and weekend events and service support on a rotating basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in workplace services, employee experience, corporate hospitality, or a related service environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience directly managing or leading a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using an FMS, service request platform, or similar system to track requests and service performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead and coach an employee-facing team in a fast-paced environment with shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong workplace service vendor management skills, including sourcing, negotiation, and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and delivering corporate events, employee programs, and meeting services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Workspace and familiarity with event planning, survey, and workplace service tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets, invoices, and service contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with minimal supervision and exercise sound judgment when handling sensitive requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple concurrent programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hospitality mindset with a track record of delivering attentive, personalized employee and guest service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; comfortable presenting and engaging at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, solutions-oriented, and calm under pressure, with strong service recovery skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to document processes and establish consistent service standards across a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to occasionally lift up to 25 lbs and perform physical tasks associated with workplace and event support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to support other workplace services priorities assigned by leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,630&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$178,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
